WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.352
In the early Yuan dynasty, the emperor decided to create a new calendar, and the astronomer Guo Shoujing accepted this great task.

00:00:08.702 --> 00:00:19.934
Later, Guo Shoujing led craftsmen to build observatories all over the country, using a huge armillary sphere to measure the positions of the stars.

00:00:20.284 --> 00:00:28.324
Every night, Guo Shoujing climbed the tall observatory, carefully observing and recording how the stars' positions changed.

00:00:28.674 --> 00:00:32.274
He observed with total concentration, often watching for an entire night.

00:00:32.624 --> 00:00:41.628
He devoted all his energy to calculation, organizing years of observation data into a new calendar.

00:00:41.978 --> 00:00:52.082
The new calendar was called the Shoushi Calendar, and it calculated the twenty-four solar terms far more accurately than before.

00:00:52.432 --> 00:01:01.264
From then on, farmers planted and harvested by the new calendar, and Guo Shoujing became a famous scientist of the Yuan dynasty.

